# open-bridge — OSS .gitignore (PUBLIC repo).
#
# This file is a DESTINATION OVERRIDE: bridge-sync writes it verbatim to
# open-bridge on every promote (see skills/bridge-sync — § Destination
# overrides). It is NOT derived from the seed's private .gitignore.
#
# --- USER-layer instance data: ignored here, re-allowed by a private origin ---
# bridge-config.yaml, ecosystem*.yaml, the lockfiles, every <id>.yaml under
# identity/ infra/ workflow/, identity/agent/*.md and work/memory/ are the part
# of a Bridge no upstream can give back, and a clone of a PUBLIC repo must never
# commit them. So they are ignored here, for every clone, before anything ran.
#
# The block below is GENERATED by `python3 scripts/user-data.py patterns` and
# held to it by scripts/tests/test_user_data.py. It names no family: until
# 2026-09-25 it listed them one by one, and a private instance that tracks its
# own data had no way back short of editing this CORE file, so a new file in a
# new place was silently left out of every commit and every backup.
#
# A PRIVATE origin re-allows it: `scripts/user-data.py arm` (run by bin/setup at
# every session start) writes identity/.gitignore, infra/.gitignore,
# workflow/.gitignore and work/.gitignore with negations. A deeper .gitignore
# wins over this one, and those files are committed with the instance, so the
# backup travels with the repo. Behind both: pre-commit refuses a credential in
# a staged instance file, pre-push refuses USER content to any remote that is
# not confirmed private (rules/push-guard.md).
# >>> user-data (managed by scripts/user-data.py, do not edit) >>>
/bridge-config.yaml
/bridge-deck.config.yaml
/ecosystem.yaml
/overlays.lock.yaml
/workspaces.lock.yaml
/context-budget.user.yaml
/edges.yaml
/reachability-scenarios.yaml
/ecosystem.*.yaml
!/ecosystem.example.yaml
/identity/*/*.yaml
/infra/*/*.yaml
/workflow/*/*.yaml
!/identity/*/_*.yaml
!/infra/*/_*.yaml
!/workflow/*/_*.yaml
/identity/agent/*.md
!/identity/agent/README.md
!/identity/agent/_*.md
/identity/designs/*.md
!/identity/designs/_*.md
/work/memory/
# <<< user-data <<<

# Overlay + workspace cache (reproducible from the lockfiles), and org rules the
# overlay materializes (reproducible from the overlay). Neither is instance data.
/.bridge/
rules/org/**
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Coverage artifacts. `coverage run` writes `.coverage` into the repo root, and
# it is a binary index of ABSOLUTE paths — so an unguarded `git add -A` after a
# coverage run puts a developer's home directory into a public PR. The leak
# check catches it, but only after the push; ignoring it is the actual fix.
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/

# Doc-system audit log — concrete filenames + persona refs = PII.
work/doc-system/

# Onboarding scan findings — discovered apps/accounts/devices = PII.
# (work/onboarding-state.yaml stays tracked on purpose — record of choices.)
work/onboarding-scan.json

# Agent-activation session state — ephemeral per session, never committed.
.bridge-active-instance

# Work system data — large historical archives + private folders stay local.
work/imports/
# Top-level imports/ — content ignored, .gitkeep stays so the dir exists.
/imports/*
!/imports/.gitkeep
# work/archive/: days/ stays local (transcripts, audio, large artifacts).
# weeks/ is tracked — canonical historical record per week.
work/archive/days/

# Secrets-bearing build artifacts — publish-profiles, connection strings.
work/tasks/**/snapshots/
work/tasks/**/publish-profile*.xml
work/tasks/**/appsettings-*.json
work/streams/**/snapshots/
work/streams/**/publish-profile*.xml
work/streams/**/appsettings-*.json

# OS files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# Editor files
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# IDE directories
.vscode/
.idea/

# Runtime artifacts
*.log
.env
.env.*
node_modules/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.pytest_cache/
.prompt.tmp

# Image-gen scratch output at repo root
generated_imgs/

# Claude
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/

# Audio files anywhere under work/ (catch-all for accidental archives)
work/**/*.wav
work/**/*.m4a
work/**/*.mp3
work/**/*.aac
work/**/*.flac
work/**/*.ogg
work/**/*.aiff
work/**/*.aif

# Bridge no-log marker — present means "skip auto-logging this session"
.bridge-nolog

# Build artifacts regenerated by daemons (dashboard / schedule / state)
work/dashboard.html
docs/repo-layout/schedule.html
work/state.json
# Runtime reports the two currency jobs rewrite on every run. Both are
# generated state, never content: upstream-autoupdate.sh shipped in #187
# without its own line, so a fresh clone that runs it grows an untracked
# file nobody put there.
work/upstream-status.md
work/overlay-status.md
work/archive-status.md

# scripts/okf-export.py output — exported bundles may contain USER PII (work/ STATUS.md, deliverables); never commit.
dist/
okf/

# Local render previews of docs/*.html, written while checking a figure in a
# headless browser. They are copies of a page with a probe script spliced in and
# have no business in the repo; three of them rode in on a `git add -A` once.
docs/_*.html

# Per-peer share folders and owner grants of a peer agent (agents/_runtime/access.py,
# skills/a2a/scripts/share_build.py): rendered output and runtime state, never content.
agents/*/share/peers/
agents/*/share/grants/
agents/*/access.grants.yaml
agents/*/.access.lock
